repository-code: "https://github.com/u00dxk2/sinusoidal-history"
abstract: >-
  Sinusoidal History overlays seven named long-wave theories of history
  (Khaldun, Kondratiev, Huntington, Perez, Turchin, Dalio, Strauss-Howe) on
  a shared 1600–2050 time axis as unit-amplitude sinusoids, each pinned to
  one explicitly documented reference peak. Six of the seven cycles are
  paired with a real long-run empirical data series for stress-testing.
  The site is an editorial comparison tool, not a forecasting instrument:
  it makes the role of calibration, theorist motivation, and selection
  effect visible by construction. Data sources are documented on the site's
  /methods page; per-source provenance is committed alongside each CSV.
keywords:
  - long-wave theory
  - cliodynamics
  - secular cycles
  - historical cycles
  - data visualization
